{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/207313-keys-ratings","id":207313,"title":"Keys...ratings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-24T10:38:45-07:00","id":207313,"title":"Keys...ratings","content":"I keep hearing references to Key ratings but when I check on the character sheet, there are no dots listed there. So is this a fault of the sheet or a system design issue or what? What am I missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T10:46:10-07:00","id":207326,"title":"","content":"In the original print of Geist the Sin Eaters, a old concept of Key Ratings was removed from the game on the whole, but wasn't properly removed from all aspects of the game. A little over a year ago, Onyx Path took all the errata compiled from the fans and revised the entire book, making a 1.1 edition. Any version of Geist you buy now has 1.1 rules, with no references to key ratings whatsoever.<br /> <br /> This does make the old one a bit of a novelty, but I believe if you contact Matt McElroy with picture proof you bought the original, a discount of some kind is offered-I think the updated PDF is at least given for free with such proof, but don't call me on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","u